w W1,W2,W3 but W2 scarce).  \n\nBetween W1 and W9:  \n- W1 has slightly better chance for chow (W2 still 2 left, W3 in hand) but still low probability.  \n- W9 has no chow except W7,W8 but W7 1 left, W8 2 left.  \n\nDiscard **W9** seems best among weak terminals.  \n\nCheck opponents\u2019 discards: in history, many terminals/honors discarded; maybe they are avoiding certain suits. Dots (B) seem less discarded, B3,B5 still many left \u2014 so keeping B4 could yield chow. Keeping T2,T8 also fine.  \n\n**Final choice:** Discard W9 to reduce terminal clutter, keep tiles with more possible connections (B4, T2, T8, W3, W1).  \n\nReason: W9 is a terminal with very few remaining tiles to form melds, and it doesn\u2019t match with other hand tiles for sequences. B4 has better potential for chow with B3 or B5 (many left). F2 pair kept for future pair requirement.  \n\n**Reason:** I choose W9 because it's the least useful tile for making melds, being a terminal with scarce remaining matching tiles, whereas keeping B4 and others offers more flexibility for forming chows.  \n\n**Answer:** Play W9"}
